+# USDC balance renders as nothing — the whole arc
+
+## TL;DR
+
+`USDC` was never registered in Scaffold-ETH's contract registry, so the
+hook read from an empty entry and quietly no-op'd. The teammate pasted it
+into the **wrong file** (`deployedContracts.ts`), which is machine-generated
+and gets rewritten on every `yarn deploy` — so the fix erased itself. USDC is
+a contract you *don't* deploy, so it belongs in **`externalContracts.ts`**,
+keyed by Base's chain id `8453`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why the hook returned `undefined` silently (no error, no request)
+
+`useScaffoldReadContract` does not read a contract directly. It first resolves
+the contract's `{ address, abi }` from Scaffold's registry:
+
+```
+useScaffoldReadContract  ->  useDeployedContractInfo("USDC")  ->  wagmi useReadContract
+```
+
+The registry is the merge of `deployedContracts.ts` + `externalContracts.ts`,
+looked up by the **target network's chain id**. When `"USDC"` isn't present
+under that chain id:
+
+- `useDeployedContractInfo` returns `data: undefined` (it just doesn't find the
+  key — it does **not** throw).
+- `useScaffoldReadContract` then calls wagmi's `useReadContract` with
+  `address: undefined` and `abi: undefined`.
+- wagmi **disables** the query when `address`/`abi` are missing (the query is
+  never `enabled`). So:
+  - no eth_call / RPC request is ever fired  → **network tab shows nothing**,
+  - no exception is thrown                    → **no runtime error**,
+  - `data` is simply never populated          → **`usdcBalance` stays `undefined`**.
+
+This is by design: Scaffold treats "contract not registered" as "nothing to
+read yet" rather than an error. The failure is a *missing registration*, not a
+bad call — which is exactly why it fails silently and why the network tab is a
+red herring.
+
+(A missing `connectedAddress` in `args` would disable the query the same way,
+but here the give-away is that registering USDC fixes it.)
+
+## 2. Why the teammate's fix worked all week, then self-destructed on deploy
+
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` is **auto-generated**. On
+`yarn deploy`, hardhat-deploy runs and a post-deploy codegen step
+(`generateTsAbis`) **overwrites the entire file** from the fresh deployment
+artifacts in `packages/hardhat/deployments/`.
+
+- Pasting a `USDC` entry there works immediately (the registry is just the
+  merged object, and the hand-added key is now in it) → "worked all week."
+- The next `yarn deploy` regenerates the file from deployment artifacts. USDC
+  is **not one of your deployed contracts** (it's Circle's token, already live
+  on Base — you never deployed it, there's no artifact for it), so it doesn't
+  make it into the regenerated file. The manual entry vanishes and the page
+  goes blank again.
+
+Rule of thumb: `deployedContracts.ts` is a build output. Never hand-edit it;
+anything you put there is temporary and dies at the next deploy.
+
+## 3. The correct registration
+
+Put third-party / already-deployed contracts (tokens, external protocols) in
+the file codegen never touches:
+
+**`packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts`**
+
+Key it by chain id. **Base mainnet = `8453`**, and native (Circle) USDC on Base
+is `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` (6 decimals).
+
+```ts
+import { GenericContractsDeclaration } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth/contract";
+
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "balanceOf",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [{ name: "account", type: "address" }],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint256" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "decimals",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "uint8" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "symbol",
+          stateMutability: "view",
+          inputs: [],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "string" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "transfer",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "to", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "function",
+          name: "approve",
+          stateMutability: "nonpayable",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "spender", type: "address" },
+            { name: "amount", type: "uint256" },
+          ],
+          outputs: [{ name: "", type: "bool" }],
+        },
+        {
+          type: "event",
+          name: "Transfer",
+          inputs: [
+            { name: "from", type: "address", indexed: true },
+            { name: "to", type: "address", indexed: true },
+            { name: "value", type: "uint256", indexed: false },
+          ],
+          anonymous: false,
+        },
+      ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- `externalContracts.ts` is **not** regenerated by `yarn deploy` — it survives.
+  Scaffold merges it with `deployedContracts.ts`, so `contractName: "USDC"`
+  resolves for both read and write hooks.
+- `as const` matters: Scaffold derives TypeScript types (function names, arg
+  types) from the literal ABI, so it gives you autocomplete/type-safety and
+  keeps `satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration` happy. A minimal ABI (just
+  `balanceOf`) is enough to unblock `/payouts`; the extra entries above let you
+  format the amount (`decimals`) and do transfers later.
+- The **chain id must match your target network.** `useDeployedContractInfo`
+  looks up by `targetNetwork.id`, so `scaffold.config.ts` `targetNetworks` must
+  include `chains.base` (8453). If you also run on Base Sepolia (84532), add a
+  `84532` block with the testnet USDC address
+  (`0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e`).
+- Result is 6-decimals raw units — divide by 1e6 (e.g. `formatUnits(bal, 6)`)
+  for display.
+
+### If you must verify the exact hook/codegen behavior in this repo
+Grep the actual sources (paths in a hardhat-flavor Scaffold-ETH 2 app):
+- `packages/nextjs/hooks/scaffold-eth/useScaffoldReadContract.ts` — confirms the
+  `useDeployedContractInfo` → wagmi `useReadContract` chain and the `enabled` gate.
+- `packages/nextjs/hooks/scaffold-eth/useDeployedContractInfo.ts` — confirms the
+  chain-id keyed lookup and the `undefined` (non-throwing) return.
+- `packages/hardhat/deploy/` + the `generateTsAbis`/`00_generate_abis` script —
+  confirms `deployedContracts.ts` is overwritten on deploy.

